0/mini-FFE3269C-9D6C-44E6-BE867A2E3E4FECF6.png","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/96E68BEC-109B-436A-BBBDA48EF20C06A0/thul-CDB3A2B5-7532-4872-B0E54D0570530DD1.png","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/96E68BEC-109B-436A-BBBDA48EF20C06A0/A539D24F-50DE-4C28-B6E7F8BC6DED8901/Guidelines-FROBT_Main Visual_Cyan_Website.png","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/96E68BEC-109B-436A-BBBDA48EF20C06A0/A539D24F-50DE-4C28-B6E7F8BC6DED8901/WebsiteJpg_XL-FROBT_Main Visual_Cyan_Website.jpg","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/96E68BEC-109B-436A-BBBDA48EF20C06A0/A539D24F-50DE-4C28-B6E7F8BC6DED8901/WebsiteWebP_L-FROBT_Main Visual_Cyan_Website.webp","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/96E68BEC-109B-436A-BBBDA48EF20C06A0/A539D24F-50DE-4C28-B6E7F8BC6DED8901/WebsiteWebP_M-FROBT_Main Visual_Cyan_Website.webp","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/96E68BEC-109B-436A-BBBDA48EF20C06A0/A539D24F-50DE-4C28-B6E7F8BC6DED8901/WebsiteWebP_XL-FROBT_Main Visual_Cyan_Website.webp","2022-06-27T10:01:13Z","Robotic Arm production lines modern industrial technology. Automated production cell.; Shutterstock ID 1722726661; purchase_order: Main Visual; job: ; client: ; other:","landscape","Caroline Sutter","2022-06-27T09:27:09Z",[],[431,432,433,434],"414FB2D4-2283-43FD-BE14E534ECA67928","6C18119B-14BD-4951-B437696F4357BD33","7C692885-DB25-4858-B1FB4FF47B241E9B","D88C0047-EC30-4506-A7DF28A4D765E1CF",[436],"frontiersin_org",[438],"Main_Visual",[440],"Photography",{"x":442,"y":443},2625,1751,[445],"Publishing","Explore open access research in robotics and AI, advancing autonomous systems, intelligence and human‑robot synergy.","\u003Cp>Frontiers in Robotics and AI is a leading multidisciplinary journal focusing on the theory of robotics, technology, and artificial intelligence, and their applications in robotic systems - from biomedical to space robotics.\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cp>Led by Field Chief Prof Editor Kostas J Kyriakopoulos (National Technical University of Athens, Greece), the journal is indexed in Scopus, Web of Science (ESCI) and the DOAJ, among others, and publishes theoretical and applied robotics research which advance technological developments to aid and enhance modern society.\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cp>Frontiers in Robotics and AI explores robotics technology across multiple, diverse disciplines from biomedical and micro-nano systems to field robotics. Featured disciplines include, but are not limited to:\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cul>\n  \u003Cli>bio-inspired robotics\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>biomedical robotics\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>computational intelligence in robotics\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>field robotics\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>haptics\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>human-robot interaction\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>humanoid robotics\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>industrial robotics\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>multi-robot systems\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>nano- and microrobotics\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>robot design\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>robot learning and evolution\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>robot vision and artificial perception\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>robotic control systems\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>soft robotics\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>space robotics.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\n\u003Cp>The journal is particularly interested in research showcasing artificial intelligence as applied to robotics, advancing perception through innovative vision and sensor systems, developing autonomous robot behavior, and establishing novel forms of interaction with the environment and humans.\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cp>The journal welcomes submissions which support and advance the UN’s Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), notably SDG 2: zero hunger; SDG 3: good health and well-being; SDG 9: industry, innovation and infrastructure; SDG 11: sustainable cities and communities; and SDG 12: responsible consumption and production.\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cp>Manuscripts that focus solely on health care practices, public health issues, or general medical studies without relevance to robotics are not suitable for publication in this journal. Military applications are out of the scope of this journal. Papers focusing on artificial intelligence must be directly applied in robotics. Similarly, studies that are primarily about human psychology or behavior, without relevance to the development or application of robotics, are also outside the scope of this journal.\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cp>Frontiers in Robotics and AI is committed to advancing developments in the field by allowing unrestricted access to articles and communicating scientific knowledge to researchers and the public alike, to enable the scientific breakthroughs of the future.\u003C/p>","cyan","3.4","4.9","51668","@FrontRoboticsAI",{"id":126,"name":127,"slug":128,"abbreviation":454,"isOnline":15,"isOpenForSubmissions":15,"impactFactor":455,"citeScore":6},"frobt",3.7,{"displayTitlePillLabels":15,"displayRelatedArticlesBox":15,"showEditors":15,"showReviewers":15,"showLoopImpactLink":15,"enableFigshare":347},{"isPublic":347,"allowCompanyUsers":347,"whiteListEmails":458,"enableAllJournals":347,"whiteListJournals":459},[],[],{"spaceId":412,"name":412,"availableJournalPages":461,"announcement":465,"useJournalPalettes":347},[254,259,256,462,463,464],"volumes","about","community-reviewers",{"__typename":466,"sys":467,"preHeader":469,"title":470,"description":471,"image":472,"link":546},"Announcement",{"id":468},"30jAeTjZfu9FwrF5jqYs9f","Our quality","Expert judgment makes science stronger","Behind every published article stand expert reviewers safeguarding science. Discover our rigorous approach to peer review.",[473],{"id":474,"src":475,"name":476,"tags":477,"type":405,"width":527,"height":528,"archive":409,"brandId":410,"limited":409,"fileSize":529,"isPublic":412,"original":530,"copyright":30,"extension":531,"thumbnails":532,"dateCreated":540,"description":476,"orientation":426,"watermarked":409,"dateModified":541,"selectedFile":30,"datePublished":542,"streamingLinks":543,"videoPreviewURLs":544,"textMetaproperties":545},"E8101B5E-CD70-402C-B234D8C42CD1D053","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/thumbnail/webimage-Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass","Doctor making notes in hospital, corona virus concept. Shot through glass.",[478,479,480,481,482,483,484,485,486,487,488,489,490,491,492,493,494,495,496,497,498,499,500,501,502,503,504,505,506,507,508,509,510,511,512,513,514,515,516,517,518,519,520,521,522,523,524,525,526],"global","professional","pandemic","conference","contagious","pneumonia","respiratory","medical","glass","exhausted","outbreak","corona","virus","making notes","writing","DOCTOR","contamination","training","Risk","Coronavirus","Science","warning","Hospital","health","close-up","infection","research","safety","prevention","concept","danger","Indoors","Disease","fever","scientist","flu","protection","men","viral","copy space","shot","Clinic","illness","healthcare","cure","seminar","epidemic","treatment","working on",4928,3280,14062390,"https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.jpg",[415],{"mini":533,"thul":534,"original":530,"webimage":475,"Guidelines":535,"WebsiteJpg_XL":536,"WebsiteWebP_L":537,"WebsiteWebP_M":538,"WebsiteWebP_XL":539},"https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/thumbnail/mini-Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/thumbnail/thul-Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/Guidelines/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.png","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/WebsiteJpg_XL/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.jpg","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/WebsiteWebP_L/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.webp","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/WebsiteWebP_M/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.webp","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/WebsiteWebP_XL/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.webp","2022-05-10T11:52:42Z","2026-02-11T15:34:30Z","2022-05-11T12:46:58Z",{},[],[],{"text":547,"url":69,"target":29,"ariaLabel":30},"Learn about peer review",{"loggedUserInfo":-1},{"currentArticle":550,"isPreviewPage":347,"hasSupplementalData":347,"showCrossmarkWidget":15,"articleTemplate":701,"currentArticlePageMetaInfo":702,"xmlParsedArticleContent":831,"xmlParsingError":-1},{"id":551,"doi":552,"title":553,"acceptanceDate":554,"receptionDate":555,"publicationDate":556,"lastModifiedDate":557,"isPublished":15,"abstract":558,"researchTopic":559,"articleType":565,"stage":568,"keywords":570,"authors":578,"editors":631,"reviewers":639,"journal":659,"section":667,"impactMetrics":669,"volume":672,"articleVolume":673,"relatedArticles":674,"isPublishedV2":15,"contents":675,"laySummary":21,"files":676},1950821,"10.3389/frobt.2026.1950821","HemiBot: design and technical validation of an adaptive Robotic coaching system for Unilateral Spatial Neglect rehabilitation",["Date","2026-09-23T14:47:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-07-28T09:23:23.000Z"],["Date","2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-11-17T02:05:16.218Z"],"IntroductionRobot-mediated neuro-motor rehabilitation offers intensive, repeatable, and objectively monitored therapy, yet existing systems rarely integrate automated session management, real-time per-repetition scoring, and data-driven adaptive difficulty progression within a single non-contact architecture. This work presents HemiBot (Hemineglect roBot), a ROS 2 software stack implementing a fully automated coaching pipeline for semicircular arm-pointing exercises on the TIAGo mobile manipulator (PAL Robotics), targeting post-stroke Unilateral Spatial Neglect (USN), in which patients fail to orient toward or interact with stimuli in the contralesional hemispace.MethodsThe robot’s end effector moves into the neglected hemispace as an exogenous attentional cue while the participant actively reaches toward it with the affected arm. The system extends a skeletal tracking framework with a Behavior Tree orchestrating exercise execution and per-repetition metric computation, a Coach node performing session-level adaptive difficulty progression, Italian empathetic text-to-speech feedback, and a scoreboard for therapist supervision. The scoring metric combines arm-alignment angle and hand–end-effector distance in a logical AND gate, yielding a normalized 0–100 score partitioned into three performance bands (Fail \u003C25, Acceptable 25–75, Great ≥75). A participant is promoted when the mean session score exceeds 75 and demoted when the fail ratio reaches 0.50. Sixteen healthy participants (mean age 54.5 ± 6.8 years) were divided into two groups of eight: a high-performance group performing all repetitions correctly, and a low-performance group following a controlled error pattern designed to trigger demotion. Kinematic time series from the robot’s onboard RGB-D camera were compared against a stereophotogrammetric gold standard (BTS SMART-DX EVO).ResultsScoring concordance between TIAGo- and mocap-derived classifications reached 100% (Cohen’s κ = 1.000) across all 120 repetitions, with no cross-band errors between Fail and Great. The executed arc trajectory showed near-perfect agreement with the commanded geometry (Pearson r > 0.99). Adaptive behavior was correct for all 16 participants.DiscussionThese findings verify that the onboard measurement chain reproduces gold-standard band assignments under the tested conditions and that the session-level decision pipeline operates end-to-end as specified. Validation of the scoring thresholds under naturally occurring, near-boundary performance remains necessary before clinical use.",{"id":560,"title":561,"articlesCount":562,"isMagazinePage":347,"slug":563,"isOpenForSubmission":347,"views":564},75675,"Robotics and Emerging Technologies in Rehabilitation: The Robot as an Assistive Tool for Both Assessment and Personalized Intervention",21,"robotics-and-emerging-technologies-in-rehabilitation-the-robot-as-an-assistive-tool-for-both-assessment-and-personalized-intervention",49983,{"id":566,"name":567},24,"Original Research",{"id":569,"name":21},18,[571,572,573,574,575,576,577],"human-robot interaction","socially assistive robotics","rehabilitation robotics","adaptive difficulty","behavior tree","TIAGo","Unilateral Spatial Neglect",[579,588,595,602,609,616,623],{"id":580,"firstName":581,"middleName":21,"lastName":582,"givenNames":583,"isCorresponding":347,"isProfilePublic":15,"userId":580,"email":-1,"affiliations":584},3402120,"Roberto","Soldi","Roberto ",[585],{"organizationName":586,"countryName":587,"cityName":21,"stateName":21,"zipCode":21},"Bioengineering Laboratory, Department of Electrical, Computer and Biomedical Engineering, University of Pavia","Italy",{"id":589,"firstName":590,"middleName":21,"lastName":591,"givenNames":592,"isCorresponding":347,"isProfilePublic":15,"userId":589,"email":-1,"affiliations":593},823353,"Bruna Maria Vittoria","Guerra","Bruna Maria Vittoria ",[594],{"organizationName":586,"countryName":587,"cityName":21,"stateName":21,"zipCode":21},{"id":596,"firstName":597,"middleName":21,"lastName":598,"givenNames":599,"isCorresponding":347,"isProfilePublic":15,"userId":596,"email":-1,"affiliations":600},3692180,"Stefania","Sozzi","Stefania ",[601],{"organizationName":